1
00:04:45,714 --> 00:04:51,714
The ocean is calling them back.

2
00:09:31,428 --> 00:09:37,428
Moana 2 is a animation, adventure, family film directed by David G. Derrick Jr..

3
00:14:17,142 --> 00:14:23,142
After receiving an unexpected call from her wayfinding ancestors, Moana journeys alongside Maui and a new crew to the far
seas of Oceania and into dangerous, long-lost waters for an adventure unlike anything she's ever faced.

4
00:19:02,857 --> 00:19:08,857
Moana (voice), played by Auliʻi Cravalho.

5
00:23:48,571 --> 00:23:54,571
Maui (voice), played by Dwayne Johnson.

6
00:28:34,285 --> 00:28:40,285
Moni (voice), played by Hualālai Chung.

7
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Loto (voice), played by Rose Matafeo.

8
00:38:05,714 --> 00:38:11,714
Kele (voice), played by David Fane.

9
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
Matangi (voice), played by Awhimai Fraser.

10
00:47:37,142 --> 00:47:43,142
Moana 2 is a 2024 American animated musical adventure film
produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios.

11
00:52:22,857 --> 00:52:28,857
The second film in the Moana franchise, it was directed by David Derrick Jr., Jason
Hand, and Dana Ledoux Miller and written by Miller and Jared Bush.

12
00:57:08,571 --> 00:57:14,571
Cast members Dwayne Johnson, Auliʻi Cravalho, Rachel House, Temuera Morrison, Jemaine
Clement, Nicole Scherzinger and Alan Tudyk reprise their roles from the first film.

13
01:01:54,285 --> 01:02:00,285
Set three years later, it follows Moana reuniting with the demigod Maui and assembling a wayfinding crew to
find the lost island of Motufetu, break its curse, and reconnect the people of the ocean.

14
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
A follow-up to Moana was originally developed as a miniseries for Disney+, but
by February 2024 it had been reworked into a theatrical sequel.

15
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
Mark Mancina and Opetaia Foaʻi, the composers and co-songwriters of the first film, returned to score
and write the songs, while Abigail Barlow and Emily Bear provided additional songs.

16
01:16:11,428 --> 01:16:17,428
Moana 2 premiered at the Lanikuhonua Cultural Institute in Kapolei, Hawaii, on November 21, 2024, and
was released by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures in the United States on November 27.

17
01:20:57,142 --> 01:21:03,142
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $1.059 billion worldwide,
outgrossing its predecessor and becoming the third highest-grossing film of 2024.

18
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
It was nominated for Best Animated Feature Film at the 82nd Golden Globe Awards.

19
01:30:28,571 --> 01:30:34,571
The film explores themes of sea, ocean, villain, musical, sequel.

20
01:35:14,285 --> 01:35:20,285
The tone is lighthearted and uplifting.
